// DS01: keep kernel and NVIDIA driver packages out of the nightly security run.
// /etc/apt/apt.conf.d/52ds01-unattended-upgrades, installed by deploy.sh.
//
// Both only take effect after a reboot. Installed nightly, a new kernel just sits
// waiting for one, and a new NVIDIA userspace against the old loaded module breaks
// nvidia-smi and every GPU container ("Driver/library version mismatch") until
// someone reboots. They upgrade in the monthly window instead
// (scripts/maintenance/monthly-update.sh), which reboots straight after.
//
// Entries are Python regexes matched with re.match, i.e. anchored at the start of
// the package name. Lists merge with 50unattended-upgrades' own (empty) blacklist.
Unattended-Upgrade::Package-Blacklist {
    "linux-";
    "nvidia-";
    "libnvidia-";
    "xserver-xorg-video-nvidia-";
};
